column20:
27/Oct/25 12:50 PM;62f15545e50f2f2a39565bf5;Hi Juri,

Thank you for being patient. the team has checked with Salesforce Support, and the following is their response.

{{I understand how important it is for you to have the ability to inline edit the Owner Full Name field in the Opportunity List View. After reviewing this further, I would like to share that this behavior is expected as per Salesforce design.  According to the official documentation, the “Owner” and “Alias” fields cannot be inline edited for any object. In addition, at the bottom of the same article, it is also mentioned that “Full Name fields on Person Accounts, Contacts, Leads, and Opportunities aren’t inline editable; however, their component fields are, such as First Name and Last Name.” This also applies to the record owner field.  For your convenience, here is the reference article: Unable to Edit Records via Inline Editing in a Salesforce List View Link: https://help.salesforce.com/s/articleView?id=000384838&type=1 }}

{{ I completely understand that this might not be the ideal experience, and I truly appreciate your understanding regarding this product limitation.}}

Regards,
Aviral Paliwal

