column17:
26/Aug/25 3:27 PM;5ebc0e69a4c57d0b8b4c78f9;{color:#172B4D}Hi Dave,{color}{color:#172B4D}{color}  

{color:#172B4D} Thanks for your quick reply.{color}{color:#172B4D}{color} 
#  
 {color:#172B4D}*Salesforce URLs* - It requires the client's Salesforce URL to submit a ticket. And our team submit about 100 tickets per day.{color} 
#  
 {color:#172B4D}*Contracts & PLI value* - We need to refer to the contract details before jumping on a call with clients, especially when the call involves some negotiation.{color} 
#  
 {color:#172B4D}*Grant Explore's access* - We will need to jump in clients' Explore to work on say searches, dashboards, manual reports, etc. It seems like the only way to access a client's Explore account is to add yourself in through Salesforce.{color} 
#  
 {color:#172B4D}*Find the POC* - Sometimes when we have a leaver on CS side, the fastest way to find the current POC internally is through SF.{color}{color:#172B4D}{color} 

  {color:#172B4D}{color} 

{color:#172B4D} I can feel our productivity took a dip since the SF switch.{color}{color:#172B4D}{color}  

{color:#172B4D} If we can find a workaround, that would be great as well!{color}{color:#172B4D}{color}  

{color:#172B4D} Thanks,{color} 
{color:#172B4D} Rio{color} 
