column19:
27/Aug/25 11:20 AM;5ebc0e69a4c57d0b8b4c78f9;{color:#172B4D}Sure!{color}{color:#172B4D}{color}  

{color:#172B4D} Just chatted with the team about the numbers — please find them below.{color} 
  {color:#172B4D}*Direct cost:* est. 239.25 USD per month (overtime for urgent requests)
  *Indirect cost:* est. 20 clients per month will need to wait an extra day for our feedback on support / reports{color} 
  {color:#172B4D}*Salesforce URLs:*
 Instead of submitting the ticket right away, we will need to wait on average another 4 hours for the URL first. Around 1% of those 100 tickets are urgent, so we will now need to work overtime to complete them on the same day. The overtime hourly rate is 22 USD, and the average ticket-solving time is 30 minutes.
 Formula: 100 tickets × 1% × 0.5h × $22 × 21.75 days = $239.25 / month{color} 
  {color:#172B4D}*Contracts & PLI value:*
 On average, we conduct 8 client calls in total. Because we often don’t have the contract in hand and can’t get back to the client during the call, around 1 client will need to wait an extra day for our feedback.{color} 
  {color:#172B4D}*Granting Explore’s access and finding POC:*
 These are harder to quantify, but they also result in longer client wait times.{color} 
{color:#172B4D} Please let me know if you have any questions.{color} 
