column19:
16/Jul/25 1:13 AM;5ebc0e68ed4a650b8e7caf9d;Hi Mukesh, 

Apologies for not being clear. Please see my notes in {color:#ff0000}red{color} below. 


When you say “My team leads need this access to be able to add people to client accounts to ensure they can get manual newsletters”, do you mean that your lead users will add the user’s email address on the Newsletter recipients on the MI Application? If they are going to work on MI Application newsletter then why they need Salesforce access?
{color:#ff0000}My two lead team members need to add our manually curated newsletter analyst team to VAS client accounts in order to curate our clients' manual newsletters. The Superadmin ID workaround only puts the account within the analyst's Fairhair for a day, and it's very time-consuming to do this every day before curation. Therefore, it would be much more efficient if they had Salesforce access and could add users to clients' Fairhair accounts permanently so they can deliver the newsletter before their contracted send time. Additionally, in instances where we need to cover sick or annual leave and need to add a new analyst to an account, then they can action this quickly and still meet the client's newsletter deadlines.{color} 

Or do you mean that they will add users for MI application via Salesforce?
{color:#ff0000}Yes, this is correct.{color}{color:#ff0000}{color} 


{color:#172B4D}Thanks,{color}
{color:#172B4D}Georgia{color}

column21:
18/Jul/25 1:39 AM;5ebc0e68ed4a650b8e7caf9d;Hi {color:#333333}Mukesh,{color}{color:#333333}{color}


{color:#333333}They also don't have access to Tatango, so could you please allocate them access?{color}{color:#333333}{color} 


{color:#333333}The company ID method only adds the account for that particular day; therefore, it only gives temporary access. Having to do this every day across multiple accounts is very time-consuming and an inefficient use of our time.{color}{color:#333333}{color}


{color:#333333}Thanks,{color}
{color:#333333}Georgia{color}{color:#333333}{color}

