column18:
08/Apr/24 7:15 PM;5dea7c237eb2280d03ca6e93;Hi Navya,



Thanks for the quick response. We have won a global RFP with Warner Brothers Discovery. In this process we’ve established a global price book including a per seat cost structure. This means that the global entity relationship with WBD will scale however the individual teams that operate within the organization are still separate operating entities. For example in this case there is a significant user group for HGTV and separately for Food Network that need their own platform access with the same level of entitlements that was purchased centrally.



Previously we could create FH instances within super admin but this is no longer available so we need your assistance in generating these instances through the SFDC integration. 



Please note in the future we will likely need additional assistance as we continue to grow the relationship with new operating groups that will be coming on board.



Let me know if anything is unclear here! Please reach out to me on Slack if needed.



Cheers,



-Mike S.





{color:#28bbbb}Michael Samuels{color}
{color:#4c4d4f}Global Director | Enterprise Client Success{color}{color:#4c4d4f}{color} 
