Hello Anna & Legal,

This is a Media Relations contact! I have now taken care of this via the [standard process outlined here|https://protect-de.mimecast.com/s/DxIZC6WDw0cmxXYGtpnoB9?domain=meltwater.atlassian.net] under "Scenario 1. Opt out" (non-GDPR). 

I share this knowing that this process was outlined in cooperation with your department; but wanting to share again because technically the data itself is not deleted (we keep the profile in an 'inactive' state which renders it undiscoverable to clients while also ensuring that it can never added again in future). 

I have created a ticket to document my actions here, which isn't necessary in GDPR but appeared to be helpful - [here|https://protect-de.mimecast.com/s/Lrp-C79ExAHN9L1WIWFC8t?domain=meltwater.atlassian.net]. 

 *Potential Action* - normally we would finish out this issue type by [sending the journalist this template to confirm|https://protect-de.mimecast.com/s/iD3qC83Gy9Iqx9pwi26CFK?domain=docs.google.com]. Can you please let me know if I should proceed with that final action, or if you would prefer to close the communication loop yourself directly?

Thanks in advance, and let me know if you have any questions!
Cheers, Michael



